            {
              "id": "kafka-rabbitmq-step-1",
              "title": "Publish, deliver and confirm",
              "description": "A shop receives one order. Read each lane as a different design for handling it. In Kafka, shipping and reporting can each replay retained orders from their own saved position. In a RabbitMQ work queue, the finished delivery leaves the queue once the worker confirms it. In Redis Streams, confirmation clears the group’s pending work and the entry stays until it is removed. Keeping past orders costs storage, but lets another team read them later. Does the shop need that history, or only the next parcel to pack?",
